  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Solve $x^{2}+16x+64=0$ and explain why it has only one solution.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-8$. Since $(x+8)^{2}=0$, both factors give the same solution.",
      "worked": "$\\begin{align*}(x+8)^{2}&=0\\\\x+8&=0\\\\x&=-8\\end{align*}$\n\nThe trinomial is a perfect square. Both factors are $x+8$, so there is only one distinct solution.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
  },
